 225:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/mbedtls/pk.h ****      * - opaque key when MBEDTLS_USE_PSA_CRYPTO is defined
 226:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/mbedtls/pk.h ****      * - normal key when MBEDTLS_PK_USE_PSA_EC_DATA is defined. In this case:
 227:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/mbedtls/pk.h ****      *    - the pk_ctx above is not not used to store the private key anymore.
 228:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/mbedtls/pk.h ****      *      Actually that field not populated at all in this case because also
 229:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/mbedtls/pk.h ****      *      the public key will be stored in raw format as explained below
 230:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/mbedtls/pk.h ****      *    - this ID is used for all private key operations (ex: sign, check
 231:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/mbedtls/pk.h ****      *      key pair, key write, etc) using PSA functions
 232:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/mbedtls/pk.h ****      *
 233:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/mbedtls/pk.h ****      * Note: this private key storing solution only affects EC keys, not the
